      "content": "<h3>getFirst, getLast and element</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Signature:</strong> <code>E getFirst();  E getLast();  E element()</code></li>\n<li><strong>Returns:</strong> the element at that end</li>\n<li><strong>Time:</strong> O(1)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>For freshers:</strong> Read the first or last element <strong>without removing</strong> it. On an empty list they throw <code>NoSuchElementException</code>. <code>element()</code> is the queue name for <code>getFirst()</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>For experienced developers:</strong> They read the <code>first</code> / <code>last</code> pointers directly. If an empty list is normal in your program, use the <code>peek</code> family (next card), which returns <code>null</code> instead of throwing.</p>",
